  "outcome": {
    "summary": "Phase 6 Phoenix trust boundary and LiveView adapter isolation gate passed narrowly; Phase 7 is eligible but not authorized.",
    "expected": "One normalized browser action reaches server-owned authentication, current-state authorization, exactly-once side effect, redacted audit, bounded result, and DOM update; denial and transport failures apply no unauthorized effect; private LiveView coupling remains removable and absent from standalone DOM, runtime, authority, Plug, and headless boundaries.",
    "observed": "The pinned browser applied two authorized counter effects across the rendered and explicit commands, replayed the second without another effect, rejected the complete governed failure matrix, delivered no disposed result, cleaned all known owned resources, retained no secret-bearing evidence, reported only exact-pin LiveView adapter eligibility with standalone fallback, and passed standalone/Plug/headless dependency isolation checks."
